{"cve": "CVE-2026-40280", "version": "N/A", "published": "2026-05-05T20:16:38.633", "lastModified": "2026-05-08T19:06:45.047", "description": "Gotenberg is an API-based document conversion tool. In versions 8.30.1 and earlier, the default private-IP deny-lists for the --webhook-deny-list and --api-download-from-deny-list flags use a case-sensitive regular expression (^https?://) to match URL schemes. Because Go's net/url.Parse() normalizes the scheme to lowercase before establishing the outbound TCP connection, an attacker can bypass the deny-list by simply capitalizing part of the URL scheme (e.g., HTTP://, HTTPS://, or Http://). This allows unauthenticated requests to reach internal network services, including private IP ranges, loopback addresses, and cloud instance metadata endpoints such as HTTP://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/. \n\nThis bypasses the same security control that was patched in CVE-2026-27018.\n\nThis issue has been fixed in version 8.31.0.", "cvssScore": 7.5, "cvsseSeverity": "HIGH", "CWE": ["441", "610", "664", "918"], "CAPEC": ["196", "219", "465", "62", "60", "664", "61", "21"], "TECHNIQUES": [{"id": "1090.001", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1134", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1134.001", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1134.002", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1134.003", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1528", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1539", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1550.004", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1606", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}], "DEFEND": [{"id": "D3-UGLPA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "User Geolocation Logon Pattern Analysis", "artifact": "Network Traffic"}, {"id": "D3-PMAD", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "Protocol Metadata Anomaly Detection", "artifact": "Network Traffic"}, {"id": "D3-CSPP", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "Client-server Payload Profiling", "artifact": "Networ